{
 "thread": "5L7KufGx6x4",
 "subject": "To exclude or not to exclude competitive models with negligible effects' covariates?",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2017-06-08T23:31:38Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "nMB-FpKXAAAJ",
   "from": "Sergio Nolazco",
   "author": "4c62fdc31c385890",
   "date": "2017-06-07T18:47:08Z",
   "subject": "To exclude or not to exclude competitive models with negligible effects' covariates?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Dear All,</b><div><br></div><div>Sometimes running distance sampling analyses for a same dataset results in many competitive models (delta AIC &lt; 2). Maybe this is a very common situation and one I am facing right now. The problem is that at the end I am interest in obtaining a single &quot;best&quot; abundance estimation and not a large set of close values from many models.   </div><div><br></div><div>In my case I got 11 models (including CDS and MCDS) with delta AICc &lt; 2. All of my models with categorical covariates other than distance did not improve the model fit enough to overcome the penalization imposed by the AICc calculation. From what I know, in this case the additional covariates have a negligible effect. In this case, it is valid or adequate to simply throw out those models and stay only with the CDS models (in which perpendicular distance is the only explanatory variable)? And then apply model averaging on those CDS models to obtain density and population estimated values? </div><div><br></div><div>The other option I am thinking about is to apply model averaging using all models (CDS and MCDS). However, some of my MCDS models got large or undesirable coefficients of variation (CV &gt; 25%) in relation to all other models. Consequently, when applying model averaging using all models I get a much larger variation and thus lower precision for my estimated values of abundance in contrast to averaging only CDS models.           </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for any opinion or comment about this matter, I am not completely sure on what option to choose or if there is another &quot;best&quot; alternative. What concerns me most is that between choosing one or other option there can be a significant difference, not in my point estimates, but in their precision.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is a table of the summary of models (ordered by increasing delta AICc). cov1 and cov2 are additional covariates other than distance.<br><div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"615\" style=\"text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;width:462pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"122\" style=\"width:92pt\">\r\n <col width=\"75\" style=\"width:56pt\">\r\n <col width=\"73\" style=\"width:55pt\">\r\n <col width=\"43\" style=\"width:32pt\">\r\n <col width=\"53\" style=\"width:40pt\">\r\n <col width=\"71\" style=\"width:53pt\">\r\n <col width=\"42\" style=\"width:32pt\">\r\n <col width=\"52\" style=\"width:39pt\">\r\n <col width=\"84\" style=\"width:63pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"22\" style=\"height:16.5pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"22\" width=\"122\" style=\"height:16.5pt;width:92pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">Covariate</span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"75\" style=\"text-align:center;width:56pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">Model</span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"73\" style=\"text-align:center;width:55pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">parameters</span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"43\" style=\"text-align:center;width:32pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">ΔAICc</span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"53\" style=\"text-align:center;width:40pt\">weights</td>\r\n  <td width=\"71\" style=\"text-align:center;width:53pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\"><font>GOF Chi</font><font>-p</font></span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"42\" style=\"text-align:center;width:32pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">CV</span></td>\r\n  <td width=\"52\" style=\"text-align:center;width:39pt\">Density</td>\r\n  <td width=\"84\" style=\"text-align:center;width:63pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">Estimate</span></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Distance+cov1</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+pol</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">3</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.15</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.68</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">25.62</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.041</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">240</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Distance+cov1</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.17</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.14</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.56</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.26</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.038</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">222</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+pol</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.37</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.12</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.74</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.28</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.040</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">238</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.60</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.11</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.62</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.17</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.037</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">220</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+cos</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.80</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.10</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.76</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">15.16</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.042</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">246</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+pol</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">3</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.35</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.08</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.76</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">15.00</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.044</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">260</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance+cov1+cov2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+pol</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">4</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.54</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.07</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.60</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">26.02</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.041</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">241</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\">Distance+cov2</span></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm+pol</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">3</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.54</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.07</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.67</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">25.55</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.041</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">239</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance+cov2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.72</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.06</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.55</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.25</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.037</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">220</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance+cov1+cov2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Hnorm</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">3</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.87</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.06</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.48</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.29</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.038</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">223</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\">Distance</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\">Unif + cos</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">1.97</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.06</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.63</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">13.84</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">0.038</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\">225</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:left;height:15pt\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\"><b>Model\r\n  averaged</b></span></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\"></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\"></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\"></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\"></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left\"></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\"><b>18.92</b></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\"><b>0.040</b></td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:center\"><b>234 (150, 330)</b></td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>MSc. Sergio Nolazco</div><div>Institute of Biosciences</div><div>University of Sao Paulo</div><div>Brazil</div></div></div></div>"
